author_journey_prompt = f"""
You extract a structured, longitudinal treatment history for GLP-1 medications from one Reddit author's posts.

OUTPUT FORMAT
- Return exactly one valid JSON object and nothing else (no markdown, no commentary).
- Follow the schema below exactly: same field names, same nesting. Do not add, drop or rename fields.
- Unavailable scalar -> null. Unavailable list -> [].
- Do not invent details. Extract only what the text supports, and keep explicit statements (explicit_notes) separate from inferences (inferred_notes).

INPUT
- All posts are from ONE author, in chronological order, each with a POST number and date.
- drug_group is provided as metadata; use it to label the drug ONLY when the specific drug is not named in the text.

WHAT TO CAPTURE
- The journey over time: drug, dose, weight/BMI, desired effects, adverse effects, adherence/access issues and confounders.
- Timing, taken from the post dates.
- An overall read of whether the evidence suggests efficacy, safety concerns, both or neither (journey_summary).

INCLUSION
{longitudinal_inclusion_rules}
Always extract desired and adverse effects even when include = false.

TIMELINE COMPLETENESS
- Produce ONE timeline_events entry for EVERY post that contains any dose, weight,
  effect, adverse event, confounder, or adherence/access information.
- Do NOT merge multiple posts into one event, and do NOT summarise the journey into
  a few representative events. A long journey must produce many events.
- Copy post_number EXACTLY from the input for each event; never invent post numbers.
- Omit a post only when it has no treatment-relevant information.

DRUG & DOSE
- Record drug names as written; map obvious misspellings to the intended GLP-1, but do not guess when unclear.
- Label every post with a GLP-1; if only drug_group is known, use that.
- Record non-GLP-1 medications as confounding_variables, never as the treatment drug.
- Capture dose transitions as concrete values (e.g. "0.25mg -> 0.5mg"), not vague phrases ("titrated up").
- drug_switching applies ONLY between two GLP-1s (e.g. Ozempic -> Wegovy). GLP-1 -> non-GLP-1 (metformin, an antidepressant) is NOT a switch.

DEMOGRAPHICS, HEIGHT, BMI
- sex_gender: parse forms like 34F / 28M and explicit words (male, female, woman, man).
- height_cm: only if explicitly stated; convert (1 in = 2.54 cm, 1 ft = 30.48 cm), else null.
- Compute bmi = weight_kg / (height_m squared) whenever both are known (1 lb = 0.453592 kg).

DATES & DURATION
- reported_treatment_duration only when explicitly quantified ("3 weeks", "2 years").
- You may infer duration from a stated start plus the post date (e.g. "started in November" + post on 2026-03-25 -> about 4 months), but do not overestimate; vague spans ("a few weeks") -> null.
- All dates as YYYY-MM-DD.

CONFOUNDERS & CO-MEDICATIONS
- Extract explicitly mentioned confounders (e.g. PCOS, diabetes, menopause, thyroid disease, ADHD, depression, steroid/peptide use, insulin resistance, diet or exercise changes, calorie deficit, pregnancy, smoking, alcohol).
- Do NOT exclude an author merely for a comorbidity or a co-medication; record these as confounders. Exclude only when the drug discussion is purely hypothetical (no personal use).

EFFECTS & SEVERITY
- Desired effects include weight loss, appetite/satiety change, reduced food noise/cravings, glucose control, improved mobility.
- Adverse effects include nausea, vomiting, constipation, diarrhea, reflux, bloating, headache, fatigue, plateau, weight regain.
- Whenever an adverse effect is present, set severity to the highest burden reported during treatment: mild (tolerable, little functional impact), moderate (impairs daily function or forces a dose change), severe (causes interruption/discontinuation, medical concern or major distress). Estimate from context if not stated.

ACTIVITY
- exercise/activity level as low / moderate / high when stated, else null.

{visualisation_grouping}

{schema_consistency_rules}

SCHEMA:
{extraction_schema}

POSTS:
{{text}}

OUTPUT:
"""
